<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9164" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏlossae</span></b> , ārum,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κολοσσαί</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Phrygia on
				the Lycus</i>, now <i>Khonas; to the church in
				this place Paul</i>'<i>s Epistle to the Colossians
				was addressed</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 32, 41, § 145</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Vulg. Col. 1,
			2</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏlos-senses</span></b> ,
				ium, m., <i>the
				Colossians</i>, <i>the inhabitants of
				Colossœ</i>, <i><span class="en">Ambros. Spir.
				Sanct. 2, 20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cŏlossīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κολοσσῖνος</span>,
				<i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Colossœ</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 9, 27, § 51</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
